{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1161","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1161","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1161\",\"parent_revision\":\"2ebf76d3c55c01a920593bf2c1b171e34c89f20b48a7a3040f7ff30e8ab86185\",\"root_revision\":\"2ebf76d3c55c01a920593bf2c1b171e34c89f20b48a7a3040f7ff30e8ab86185\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nBacklogItem.sections was added as a structured field (P964 Gap 1, commit c4d33c09) but no consuming agents have been updated to know it exists or how to use it. All agents that read backlog items currently see only description and frontmatter metadata \u2014 the sections content is invisible to them.\\n\\nThe intended access pattern is progressive disclosure: agents receive the item description and frontmatter as initial context, then load sections on-demand by name based on their pipeline stage. A planning agent loads RT-ICA and Fact Check sections. A verification agent loads Learnings sections. Neither loads everything.\\n\\nFor this routing to work, agents need: (1) to know sections exist and how to query them, (2) a section index readable without loading section content, so the agent can decide what to load before spending context budget. A SectionType field on Section (or a well-known key registry) is required to make section types discoverable by stage without reading section bodies.\\n\\nWhat is missing: the agent skill files that consume backlog items (groom-backlog-item, work-backlog-item, rt-ica, feature-researcher, etc.) have no instructions for sections access. The backlog_view MCP tool returns sections in its response but agents are not told to use them.\\n\\nImpact: all structured data added to BacklogItem.sections (RT-ICA results, impact radius, learnings, fact checks) is effectively hidden from every agent that processes backlog items. The migration added the field but left the consumer side incomplete.\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-11)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n9/10 \u2014 All agents in the development harness pipeline that read backlog items (groom-backlog-item, work-backlog-item, feature-researcher, and the rt-ica skill) currently receive zero structured sections data. The BacklogItem.sections field exists in the model and backlog_view returns it, but no agent is told how to access it. Every groomed section (RT-ICA results, impact radius, fact checks, learnings) written to an item is invisible to every downstream agent.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: All agents that need to consume previously-groomed structured data (fact-check results, RT-ICA outcomes, impact radius, learnings) from backlog items\\n- Bottleneck: grooming an item produces structured sections that cannot be consumed \u2014 agents must re-derive data already captured in sections because they do not know the sections exist\\n- Affects agents: @dh:backlog-item-groomer, @dh:feature-researcher, @dh:fact-checker, @dh:impact-analyst, and any pipeline stage agent that loads a backlog item\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Agents can load only the sections relevant to their pipeline stage (progressive disclosure), avoiding unnecessary context budget on sections they do not use\\n- Structured data persisted in items (RT-ICA assessments, fact-check verdicts, impact radius) becomes reusable across sessions and agents\\n- Grooming becomes cumulative: a re-groomed item retains prior fact-check and RT-ICA sections that future agents can query without re-running the analysis\\n- Enables the consumer side of the BacklogItem.sections feature introduced in P964, completing the producer-consumer contract\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen an agent receives a backlog item to work on, it calls `backlog_view(selector, summary=True)` first to get the `sections_index` \u2014 a compact list of section names with entry counts. The agent reads the index to decide which sections are relevant to its pipeline stage, then calls `backlog_view(selector, summary=False, section=\\\"SectionName\\\")` to load only those sections. An agent in the grooming stage loads `Groomed` sections. An agent doing RT-ICA loads `RT-ICA` sections if present. A verification agent loads `Learnings` sections. No agent loads the full body unless it needs the raw text for a specific reason.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nEach consuming agent skill file or agent prompt gains a documented access pattern for BacklogItem.sections. The pattern covers: (1) call `backlog_view` with `summary=True` to get `sections_index`; (2) inspect `sections_index` to identify relevant sections by name; (3) call `backlog_view` with `summary=False` and `section=` to load specific named sections. The pattern is documented in the `/dh:backlog` skill reference and cross-referenced from each affected agent file. No new MCP tool is required \u2014 the existing `backlog_view` `summary` and `section` parameters are the interface.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. The `/dh:backlog` skill (`plugins/development-harness/skills/backlog/SKILL.md`) documents the progressive disclosure access pattern: `summary=True` for index, then `summary=False` with `section=` for targeted load\\n2. The `@dh:backlog-item-groomer` agent (`plugins/development-harness/agents/backlog-item-groomer.md`) includes instructions to check `sections_index` before loading sections and to load prior groomed sections (e.g. `Fact Check`, `RT-ICA`) when they exist, to avoid re-deriving already-captured data\\n3. The `/dh:work-backlog-item` skill and its routing workflows reference the sections access pattern when loading item context for planning\\n4. The `@dh:feature-researcher` agent includes instructions to load `RT-ICA` and `Fact Check` sections from the item if they exist before starting its research\\n5. None of the updated agents load the full item body when only section content is needed (verified by inspecting updated prompts)\\n6. A smoke test: groom an item with a `Fact Check` section; invoke `@dh:feature-researcher` on it; confirm the agent's output references the pre-existing fact-check data rather than re-deriving it\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| File | plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/models.py \u2014 BacklogItem.sections at line 846, ViewItemResult.sections_index at line 1099 |\\n| File | plugins/development-harness/agents/backlog-item-groomer.md \u2014 primary agent to update |\\n| File | plugins/development-harness/agents/feature-researcher.md \u2014 agent to update |\\n| File | plugins/development-harness/agents/fact-checker.md \u2014 agent to update |\\n| File | plugins/development-harness/agents/impact-analyst.md \u2014 agent to update |\\n| File | plugins/development-harness/skills/backlog/SKILL.md \u2014 reference skill to update with access pattern |\\n| File | plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/SKILL.md \u2014 skill to update |\\n| Skill | /dh:backlog \u2014 documents MCP tool parameters including include_content, section, summary |\\n| Issue | #1162 \u2014 prerequisite: SectionType on SectionMeta for stage-based routing (status: groomed) |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: #1162 (Add SectionType to Section model) \u2014 must be groomed and implemented first so agents can filter sections by type rather than relying on name-matching alone. #1161 can document name-based access in the interim, but stage-based routing requires #1162.\\n- Blocks: None identified \u2014 this is a leaf item in the current backlog\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nMedium \u2014 Requires reading and editing multiple agent prompt files and skill references (5\u20137 files). No code changes to `backlog_core`. The access pattern is already functional in the MCP tool (`backlog_view` with `summary=True`/`section=` params are implemented); this is purely agent instruction documentation work. Risk: determining the right level of detail in each agent's prompt without over-specifying the pattern.\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **agents not updated to use backlogitem.sections \u2014 progressive disclosure access pattern missing** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 fix-append-or-replace agent research, 2026-03-31\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-01\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"03ae3cac5791f1e2ce1b3fa5cae0cd1f6ca0a8f6ff534ed980cef9c7d728e3e6\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPS8q7g\"}"}